Near miss for prefer_exitcase and exitcase_after_return: every branch ends
with :RETURN as its final statement (a trailing comment is transparent),
so no :EXITCASE is needed and none is unreachable (issue #139;
diag.prefer_exitcase, diag.exitcase_after_return "Does not flag").
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE GradeFor;
	:PARAMETERS nScore;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE nScore >= 90;
		:RETURN "A";
	:CASE nScore >= 75;
		:RETURN "B";
	:OTHERWISE;
		:RETURN "C";
		/* scores below 75 all share one grade;
	:ENDCASE;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE GradeFor;
	:PARAMETERS nScore;
	:BEGINCASE;
	:CASE nScore >= 90;
		:RETURN "A";
	:CASE nScore >= 75;
		:RETURN "B";
	:OTHERWISE;
		:RETURN "C";
		/* scores below 75 all share one grade;
	:ENDCASE;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
